  "summary": "Cyberminimalism (or Cyberbougie ) is a hyper-minimalistic aesthetic that arose in the late 2010s.",
  "description": "Cyberminimalism (or Cyberbougie ) is a hyper-minimalistic aesthetic that arose in the late 2010s. It pushed beyond Flat Design 's minimalism into an even more reductive design style. At its most extreme, it is composed of sans-serif words, color gradients, a design grid and little to nothing else. Originally confined to the web and tech spaces, it later spread into other industries.",
